 "source": "Original map data created for Backstabplomacy for Raphael's Armenian church play group. The Caucasus is one of the great under-represented boards in strategy gaming: seven peoples between two seas, one mountain spine, and everybody's empire has marched through it. Centres: Yerevan, Artsakh and Gyumri for Armenia; Tbilisi, Kutaisi and Batumi for Georgia; Baku, Ganja and Shirvan for Azerbaijan; Constantinople, Trabzon and Van for Turkey (yes, someone has to play Turkey \u2014 draw lots, loser gets the Bosphorus); Tabriz, Tehran and Gilan for Persia; Krasnodar, Crimea and Makhachkala for Russia; Athens, Thessaloniki and Crete for Greece. Kars, Derbent and Cyprus start neutral.",
